<html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Meeting Summary</title></head><body><div class=""><strong>Meeting Summary</strong><p></p><p><strong>Executive Summary</strong><br>The meeting covered project updates, discussed timelines, and set decisions for the upcoming sprint. The team reviewed progress on backend, frontend, QA, and DevOps, and addressed open issues.</p><p><strong>Key Points Discussed</strong></p><p>* Backend: Completed new endpoints for user profile management, awaiting QA testing and review<br>* Frontend: New profile page UI nearing completion, with state management and react-query integration<br>* QA: Tested auth flows and profile API endpoints, reported bugs, and planned Cypress tests<br>* DevOps: CI pipeline stable, added checks for secrets in logs, and set up auto-deployment to staging<br>* Timeline: Targeting feature freeze by July 5th, with a backup plan for analytics module<br>* Next Sprint: Focus on admin portal features, with tickets and spec doc available</p><p><strong>Decisions Made</strong></p><p>* Target feature freeze by July 5th, with a buffer day on July 3rd for QA<br>* Create a backup plan for analytics module using dummy data<br>* Standardize commit messages using conventional commits<br>* Enforce commit message format in CI using a pre-commit hook</p><p><strong>Action Items</strong></p><p>* Raj:<br>	+ Fix environment variable fallback on JWT_SECRET<br>	+ Fix validation issue causing 500 error on email field update<br>* Lina:<br>	+ Complete state management for form submission<br>	+ Check Lighthouse for performance and bundle size impact<br>	+ Integrate updated form field specs from UX team<br>* Michael:<br>	+ Complete Cypress tests for profile UI by Thursday<br>* Ethan:<br>	+ Review Raj's PR for backend endpoints<br>	+ Set up new namespace and DB schema for admin roles<br>	+ Add pre-commit hook for commit message format<br>* Sarah:<br>	+ Create dummy data and placeholders for analytics module<br>* Alice:<br>	+ Update onboarding doc with standardized commit message format<br>	+ Send out action items and meeting summary by EOD</p><p><strong>Next Steps</strong></p><p>* Review and address open issues and action items<br>* Prepare for next sprint, focusing on admin portal features<br>* Reconvene on Monday, same time, to review progress and discuss further</p><p><strong>Open Questions</strong></p><p>* Will the external vendor provide SDK updates on time for the analytics module?<br>* Are there any potential blockers for the July 5th feature freeze deadline?</p><p><strong>Emotional Insight</strong><br>The meeting had a productive and collaborative tone, with team members actively discussing and addressing open issues. There was a sense of urgency around meeting the July 5th deadline, but the team seemed motivated to work together to achieve it. The discussion around standardized commit messages and CI pipeline improvements showed a focus on process improvement and attention to detail. Overall, the meeting was well-structured and efficient, with clear action items and next steps.</p></div></body></html>